jobs.description:
&lt;h3&gt;About Enterpret&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the world moves to AI native applications, one element matters more than anything: the data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Enterpret, we are unlocking the most impactful dataset for businesses, customer feedback. We centralize feedback across every source, like Twitter, Salesforce, Zendesk, Slack, Intercom, community forums, surveys, and Gong calls, into a single knowledge graph. On top of it we build an adaptive taxonomy for each customer and an agent platform that lets teams query, monitor, and act on customer intelligence wherever they work, whether that&#39;s inside Enterpret, in Slack, or in their own AI tools through our MCP server.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include companies like Canva, Harvey, Zapier, WisprFlow, ElevenLabs, OpenRouter, Western Union, and several other Product Led Growth decacorns and F500 companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enterpret is looking for a sharp, data-driven operator to drive high-impact strategic and operational initiatives across the company, with a primary focus on revenue operations and business systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of our BizOps team reporting to the Chief of Staff to the Co-Founder, whose portfolio spans Business Operations and Product Operations, you will operate at the intersection of operations, finance, and GTM as a trusted problem solver and thought partner to teams across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, high-autonomy role for an experienced individual contributor who enjoys solving hard problems and building systems that work. You will understand priorities, recommend solutions and take work from an unclear starting point to a working result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own and improve the workflows that connect our Sales, Marketing and Customer Success teams. This includes how leads reach the right person, how opportunities move through the pipeline, how teams use reliable data and how approved commercial terms flow into operational systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use AI as part of how we work. We want someone who can use it to learn, analyse, build and automate, while staying accountable for accuracy and quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why this role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have real ownership of revenue workflows and the autonomy to improve how they work. Working directly with the Chief of Staff and closely partnering with the Head of Revenue and CEO, you will shape the systems behind our revenue operations and see the impact of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify problems in our revenue workflows, recommend what matters most and own improvements through to measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve core revenue workflows, including lead routing, opportunity management, renewals and the handoffs between teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand our CRM and connected systems well enough to find the cause of issues, fix them safely and prevent them from recurring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep revenue data reliable. Define metrics clearly, reconcile conflicting records and build reporting people can use to make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pipeline reviews, forecasting and quarterly planning with accurate inputs, clear risks and useful recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Finance and commercial teams to keep approved deal terms, subscription records and billing handoffs aligned. Help resolve exceptions without making policy or financial commitments on your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build useful automations and AI-assisted workflows. Test them with real users, monitor their results and improve them after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional work forward. Agree on owners and dates, raise blockers early and bring the right people together when a decision is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leave behind clear documentation and maintainable systems, not solutions that depend on one person remembering how they work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning revenue operations, business systems or closely related operational work. You can show work you personally took from problem to result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a CRM such as Salesforce or HubSpot and the workflows around it. You can explain more than the dashboard layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills. You are comfortable working with spreadsheets and SQL, checking data quality and explaining what the numbers mean.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to build and troubleshoot integrations or automations using APIs, tools such as n8n or Zapier, or lightweight code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical use of AI tools and agents, with a clear method for checking their output and measuring whether they help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity, sound judgment and the ability to learn unfamiliar systems quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communication and the confidence to work directly with people across teams and levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of following through. You keep people informed and verify that a change actually worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome relevant experience from different backgrounds. The strongest evidence is the work you have owned and the judgment you brought to it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why Enterpret&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the heaviest data systems in the company — the databases, models, and pipelines behind the product — at the moment the scale story gets much more interesting: larger enterprise customers and large-scale PLG volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; End-to-end responsibility for features and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Challenges:&lt;/strong&gt; Make hard-to-reverse, 1–2 year architecture decisions across distributed databases, model hosting, and high-throughput pipelines, where a single change touches storage, query paths, reliability, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead future programs such as self-hosting and regional expansion to Europe and India, with an open L6 IC path for someone who can own long-term platform strategy and raise the bar across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture:&lt;/strong&gt; Open, collaborative, and values-driven environment with autonomy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive salary, equity, hybrid work setup, premium healthcare, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We Value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Enterpret, we operate with a deep sense of ownership — we play for the team and do what it takes to win together. We care personally for our teammates while pushing each other with honest, actionable feedback. Above all, we approach everything with humility and a drive to keep learning and getting better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Equal Opportunities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer. We ensure that none of our employees or prospective employees receives less favourable treatment as a result of age, sex, disability, marital status, colour, race, religion or ethnic origin. Equally we aim to ensure that no such employee is disadvantaged by terms and conditions of employment which cannot be justified.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Coursera + Udemy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coursera and Udemy are now one company, bringing together two mission-driven brands to create the world’s most powerful platform for turning learning into progress. Together, we help more than 300 million learners and 12,000+ enterprise customers build the skills they need for a world being reshaped by AI. Read more about the combined company by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.coursera.org/coursera-and-udemy-are-now-one-company-creating-the-worlds-most-comprehensive-skills-platform/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us now?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is transforming how people learn, work, and grow, and the need for new skills has never been greater. Coursera brings trusted content and credentials from leading university and industry partners, while Udemy brings a dynamic skills marketplace and global network of real-world experts. By combining these strengths, we can connect more people and organizations to the skills they need, when they need them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape what comes next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our team, you’ll have the opportunity to reshape how the world learns and applies skills—and help millions of people participate in the new economy. Bring your ideas, expertise, and perspective to meaningful work that can make a difference at global scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coursera is seeking an AI Specialist to design and build AI systems that transform ambiguous business problems into working prototypes and measurable solutions. You&#39;ll work across the full lifecycle of applied AI—from data exploration and experimentation through deployment—selecting the right combination of techniques, models, and architectures for each challenge. This is a hands-on role where you&#39;ll architect retrieval pipelines, agentic workflows, and evaluation frameworks while collaborating closely with Product Managers, Data Analysts, Software Engineers, and the business teams who use what you build. You&#39;ll be deeply technical with modern LLM and GenAI systems, equally comfortable training custom models, designing RAG pipelines, and pushing the boundary of what AI can do for education.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About your skills:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Science - Core discipline for extracting insights from structured and unstructured data using scientific methods and algorithms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Pipelines - Essential for designing and managing series of AI processing steps from data ingestion through model inference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI Fluency - Understanding capabilities and limitations of LLMs, embeddings, and AI tools to apply them appropriately to problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and design AI systems by selecting the right combination of data, retrieval pipelines, agentic workflows with tool use, and structured extraction from unstructured sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines with vector databases such as Pinecone or Weaviate for grounded, context-aware AI applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain agentic AI workflows using frameworks such as Langgraph, Mastra, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, or AutoGen, including multi-step tool use, planning, and autonomous execution loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run evaluation for every AI system you ship, covering accuracy, hallucination and grounding checks, regression suites, and human review loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with large-scale structured and unstructured datasets on cloud-native databases and storage such as S3, Postgres, GCS, BigQuery, and Databricks, with strong SQL and data modeling skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build rapid AI prototypes and experiment with different models, retrieval strategies, prompts, and approaches to find what works best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in Data Science, Applied AI, or Machine Learning, with experience building data-driven or AI-powered solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking an AI use case from data exploration and experimentation through a validated working prototype.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with machine learning and modern Generative AI techniques such as LLMs, embeddings, RAG, semantic search, NLP, recommendation systems, or agentic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 production deployments involving LLM-based systems including fine-tuning, RAG, agentic workflows, or prompt-engineered solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI experimentation and evaluation, including comparing approaches, defining quality metrics, analyzing errors, and iterating based on results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of identity and access management, encryption and key management, and secure network patterns such as VPC peering, PrivateLink, and mTLS for customer-embedded or regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Python and SQL to work with data, build analysis workflows, develop AI algorithms, experiment with models, and build AI and ML solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information about how Coursera collects and uses your personal information, please see our &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.clinchtalent.com/1d7f2c0f91ebf75d580f56447fa54859/2acb24eb91f1e23b90ac9e9285de5aaf/Global%20Applicant%20Privacy%20Notice.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Coursera + Udemy Global Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect against recruitment fraud, Coursera + Udemy recruiters only communicate via official coursera.org/udemy.com email addresses and never through personal accounts. We do not accept resumes via email or social media; please submit all applications directly through our careers page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you encounter suspicious recruitment activity, please report it via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/Mb8UktwuaJAukb3H7&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Submission Form.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coursera is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building a welcoming and inclusive workplace. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to legally protected characteristics and provide reasonable accommodations upon request at recruiting@coursera.org.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

