&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Notice to prospective HackerRank job applicants:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our Recruiters use @hackerrank.com email addresses.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;We never ask for payment or credit check information to apply, interview, or work here.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join the Future of Security at Netskope&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netskope (NASDAQ: NTSK) is a leader in modern security and networking for the cloud and AI era. We secure and accelerate cloud, data, and AI in real time, everywhere. Thousands of customers, including more than 30 of the Fortune 100, trust the Netskope One platform, its Zero Trust Engine, and the powerful NewEdge network to gain full visibility and control without performance trade-offs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netskope, our technology is driven by our greatest strength: our people. We believe that belonging powers innovation, and success is both personal and organizational. We embrace differences in gender, ethnicity, beliefs, ability, and identity, creating an environment where every voice is heard and respected. We empower our employees to bring their authentic selves to work, grow their careers through continuous education and mentorship, and lead with transparency and curiosity. Join a team where you belong, where you are encouraged to be an entrepreneur, and where together, we continue to redefine the landscape of security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.netskope.com/company/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Careers at Netskope&lt;/a&gt; to learn more. Follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/netskope&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/netskope/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note, this team is hiring across all levels and candidates are individually assessed and appropriately leveled based upon their skills and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netskope SASE Quality Engineers ensure the delivery of high-performance, scalable WAN edge and Cloud networking solutions. Driven by an automation-first and customer-centric approach, you will design and execute comprehensive tests—from feature-specific validation to complex, system-level scale—to guarantee flawless software delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be a key member of the SASE team, championing quality and automation for our advanced WAN edge and Cloud networking products in a fast-paced, high-impact environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the product/feature requirement, review the design and write test plans that suits the customer use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible to own a feature end to end -&amp;nbsp; starting from testing, automation, script error free run in regression and customer issues handling around that&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of the product features and building the ability to debug the customer issues and suggest/implement the workarounds if applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need to perform different types of testing that includes functional, system, performance and scale tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need to create the distributed complex test setups in various cloud platforms and hypervisors based on the requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross functional teams at various stages of product development to meet the feature deliverables in a release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant experience in software testing, quality engineering, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in one or more of the Windows, macOS, Linux and Android platforms, with experience testing system-level agents(VPN clients, or SASE/SSE clients ) in large-scale enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge to bring up test environments, testing, automation&amp;nbsp; and troubleshooting in Windows/macOS and Linux platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in L2/L3 networking concepts, routing protocols, VPN, IPSec and WAN architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in python programming language and should be able to do automation driven testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Docker, Kubernetes environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with one of the major server virtualisation products (ESXi, KVM) &amp;amp; IaaS platforms (Azure, AWS, GCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good working knowledge in CI/CD deployment in public clouds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical know-how of source code systems like Github&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with traffic generator tools like Spirent and Ixia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in scale and performance validation of endpoint client deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with web programming and HTTP based APIs (REST or GraphQL)&lt;/li&gt;
